        "title": "Mirror ten Desktop placements into Web chat inventory",
        "summary": "A new module in `common/src/ads/web-desktop-placements.ts` maps ten Desktop ad slots (inline, breaks, partner, and billboard) to Web-only variants ending in the `:web` suffix. The shared placement registry in `common/src/constants/freebuff-placements.ts` now computes `PLACEMENT_SLOTS` by appending these web aliases to the original Desktop and mobile slots, giving them the `freebuff_web_chat` surface. The billboard module resolves web aliases back to their Desktop source so artwork requirements and shape checks apply identically to both variants. Campaign targeting logic treats a web alias as a target only if its Desktop source is explicitly targeted, preventing arbitrary suffixes from expanding campaign reach.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "advertisers",
        "evidence": "New file `common/src/ads/web-desktop-placements.ts` defines `WEB_DESKTOP_SOURCE_PLACEMENTS` and helper functions like `desktopPlacementSource`; `common/src/constants/freebuff-placements.ts` renames the static list to `ORIGINAL_PLACEMENT_SLOTS` and computes `PLACEMENT_SLOTS` by appending web-mirrored entries via `webDesktopPlacement`, while `common/src/ads/billboard.ts` updates `billboardShapesForPlacement` to resolve web aliases through `desktopPlacementSource`.",
        "userVisible": false,
